#: includes/class-cleanup-report-optimization.php:178
msgid "Mobiles have fewer hardware and software resources, which reflects directly on the browser's performance. Any metric used in performance tests affects the score more drastically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-cleanup-report-optimization.php:179
msgid "Why target 80 for mobile?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-cleanup-report-optimization.php:180
msgid "Google considers anything 90+ a good score, but it also explains that a good score doesn't mean a good user experience: Google uses the 75th percentile as the goal for a page to work well for the majority of users."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-cleanup-report-optimization.php:181
msgid "Why is my score different from the ones in this report?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-cleanup-report-optimization.php:182
msgid "There are many reasons for a score to change, but the most common are:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-cleanup-report-optimization.php:184
msgid "<strong>Location:</strong> Google uses your location to decide where the page is tested from. There are 3 networks (Asia, North America and Europe); it doesn't specify the countries. We use a connection to the location closest to your server, so testing from a different location can give a different result. Cloudflare or another CDN can help make results more stable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-cleanup-report-optimization.php:185
msgid "<strong>Big changes in the website:</strong> the optimization is done on the website as it is. Changing the layout or the settings we defined can affect the score."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-cleanup-report-optimization.php:187
msgid "Core Web Vitals say \"Failed\""
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-cleanup-report-optimization.php:188
msgid "Core Web Vitals can say \"Failed\" even after optimization and a good PageSpeed Insights (PSI) score. PSI simulates the user experience, while Core Web Vitals rely on real user data: it can take 28+ days for them to update, and a good PSI score doesn't guarantee passing Core Web Vitals because real-world conditions differ."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-cleanup-report-optimization.php:189
msgid "Two key factors are server location (is it close to your audience?) and traffic (is there enough data for Google to assess?). If these are addressed and Core Web Vitals still fail, further investigation is needed: a deeper look at real user performance data and field data issues, and possibly structural changes to the website."
msgstr ""

